# Eyes Day: the day theme for long sessions in a lit room (formerly
# Antigravity), modelled on Antigravity IDE's Solarized Light.
# It keeps that theme's cream ground #fdf6e3, its soft surface #eee8d5 (slot 7)
# and the eight Solarized hue families, tuned for comfort (sources in
# references/themes.md):
# - Dark text on a light ground reads sharper in daylight (Buchner 2007,
#   Piepenbrock 2013). Text is warm charcoal #353129 at 12:1 (lightened from 14:1
#   at the user's request) instead of true black at 19:1; more contrast adds no reading speed (Legge 1987).
# - Seven clearly separate hue families, each normal/bright pair one family
#   apart only in lightness (red 1/9, orange 4, ochre-gold 3/11, green 2,
#   teal 6/10, blue 12/14, purple 5/13), chroma 0.08-0.15: varied like
#   Fahrenheit or Standardpin without near-duplicate hues, never neon; normal slots sit in one band at
#   5.8:1 (red 6.6:1, the orange 4.6:1) and bright slots at 4.3-5.1:1.
# - Slot 4 carries Fahrenheit's rust orange (#cb4a05 darkened a hair to
#   4.6:1) instead of blue, because Claude Code draws inline code in slot 4
#   and the user chose that orange for it; slot 12 keeps a clear blue (Herdr
#   done). Slot 10 is a Solarized-style teal because Claude Code colors code
#   strings with it (green covered whole JSON files); 6 is its deeper pair. Slot 1 is a clear red (chroma 0.15) so blocked and errors
#   separate from the ochre accent.
# - One accent: the cursor takes slot 3 ochre, matching the active tab and
#   Claude Code's selection (theme-overrides/eyes-day.toml). Cursor text is a bright
#   orange #ff9d42 (3.0:1 on the block): Claude Code draws the voice level at
#   the cursor in this color, and cream there read as the ground filling up.
# - Extended slots 22 and 52 carry soft green and brick tints for Claude Code's
#   added/removed diff rows, and 28 and 88 the changed words in the same hues
#   three steps deeper (#b7d19d, #edb9a8; 1.35:1 off the row), the strength
#   every theme uses (user; a same-color word layer was dropped here before as
#   clutter, the deeper same-hue step was chosen from a preview). Body text
#   reads above 11:1 on the rows and 7.5:1 on the words (theme-overrides/eyes-day.toml).
# - One selection color everywhere: the ochre wash #e6d6b7 (Ghostty selection,
#   Claude Code selectionBg, Herdr selected row), 1.33:1 off the ground.
# - Slot 8 is secondary text at 4.5:1, kept clearly lighter than body text
#   (2.65:1 apart; at 6:1 the two read alike), 15 is paper. Faint text is 85%
#   opacity: at 70% Claude Code's dimmed removed diff lines read 5.3:1 beside
#   13:1 added lines; 85% gives 7.8:1, still visibly lighter.
# - Text uses the global Medium weight like every other theme (SemiBold was
#   tried here and read too heavy).
# - Extended slot 230 carries the body text #353129 for the Claude Code status
#   line, which dims default-colored text to grey.
